{
  "name": "Timeline for a Typical Preventive Roof Inspection",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1: Initial Consultation and Scheduling (1-2 Days)",
      "text": "This is where you reach out to a trusted professional like Discounted Roofing Co. We'll discuss your concerns, the age of your roof, and any recent weather events. We'll then schedule a convenient time for a detailed inspection. This phase is about gathering initial information and setting expectations.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 2: On-Site Visual Assessment (1-2 Hours)",
      "text": "Our inspector will arrive at your home and conduct a thorough visual examination of your roof from the ground, looking for obvious signs of wear, damage, or debris. We'll also check gutters for granule buildup and look at exterior walls for water stains. This initial scan helps us identify areas that need closer attention.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 2
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 3: Detailed Roof Surface Inspection (1-3 Hours)",
      "text": "Next, our team will safely access your roof to examine it up close. This involves checking shingles for cracks, curls, or missing pieces, inspecting flashing around chimneys and vents, assessing seams, and looking for any signs of water penetration or structural issues. We'll also take photos to document any findings.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 3
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 4: Attic and Interior Check (30 Minutes - 1 Hour)",
      "text": "If accessible, we'll inspect your attic for signs of moisture, leaks, or inadequate ventilation. We'll also check ceilings inside your home for any subtle water stains that might indicate a roof issue. This step connects the dots between external roof conditions and internal home impact.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 4
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 5: Report and Recommendations (1-2 Days After Inspection)",
      "text": "After the on-site work, we'll compile a detailed report summarizing our findings, including photographic evidence. We'll then present this to you, explaining any defects, their probable causes, and prioritizing recommended repairs. We'll discuss your options, whether it's minor repairs or a full replacement, and provide transparent pricing for any proposed work. This step ensures you have all the information needed to make an informed decision for your home.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 5
    }
  ],
  "@type": "HowTo",
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "speakable": {
    "@type": "SpeakableSpecification",
    "cssSelector": [
      "h1",
      ".howto-step",
      "[itemprop=\"step\"]"
    ]
  },
  "totalTime": "PT30M",
